<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martín Delgado</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1858">1858</a>–<a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Martín Teófilo Delgado</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Martín Delgado was a Filipino general from Iloilo who led the revolution against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> on Panay in 1898. His forces besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iloilo-city">Iloilo City</a> until the Spanish garrison surrendered on 25 December 1898, and he led revolutionary forces on Panay against the Americans in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a>. After surrendering in 1901 he became the first civil governor of Iloilo province under American rule.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martin-delgado.jpg" alt="Martín Delgado" width="320" height="402" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Fdelrosario · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gen._Mart%C3%ADn_Te%C3%B3filo_Delgado_y_Bermejo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
